sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  box rgb(227,242,253) People and cockpit
    actor AU as Author (pricing manager or analyst)
    participant CK as Cockpit
    actor AP as Approver (compliance officer)
    actor AD as Auditor or support staff
  end
  box rgb(232,245,233) Host service
    participant HS as Host business code
    participant RE as Rule Engine
    participant DB as Host PostgreSQL
  end

  Note over AU,RE: Author
  AU->>CK: Import draft v2 (YAML or JSON)
  CK->>RE: Create version v2, Idempotency-Key
  RE->>RE: Validate rows and types
  alt Ill-typed row
    RE-->>CK: 422 with row id, v2 stays DRAFT
  else Valid
    RE->>DB: Store v2 as DRAFT
  end

  Note over AU,RE: Simulate
  AU->>CK: Paste sample inputs
  CK->>RE: Simulate v2 next to effective v1
  RE-->>CK: Outcomes per row, changed outcomes marked, no log writes

  Note over AU,AP: Request
  AU->>CK: Request publication, effectiveFrom 1 Feb 2027
  CK->>RE: Request publication
  RE->>DB: v2 to PENDING_APPROVAL, event publish-requested
  RE-->>AP: Pending approval (cockpit queue or event)

  Note over AP,RE: Approve
  AP->>CK: Open diff of v1 and v2
  alt Approver is the author
    CK->>RE: Approve
    RE-->>CK: 403 SELF_APPROVAL_FORBIDDEN, v2 stays PENDING_APPROVAL
  else Different identity
    CK->>RE: Approve
    RE->>DB: v2 PUBLISHED with effectiveFrom
  else Reject with comment
    CK->>RE: Reject
    RE->>DB: Draft returned to the author
  end

  Note over RE,DB: Effective date
  RE->>RE: Every replica serves v2 from effectiveFrom, cache coherent within 5 s

  rect rgba(232,245,233,0.6)
    Note over HS,DB: Evaluate in the business transaction (one TX)
    HS->>RE: evaluate(card-fee, inputs, clock)
    RE-->>HS: Outputs, version v2, matched row R2
    HS->>DB: Business write
    RE->>DB: Decision log insert (masked inputs as keyed hash)
    Note over HS,DB: Commit, or rollback removes both
  end

  Note over AD,RE: Explain
  AD->>CK: Open decision by id or filter
  CK->>RE: Get decision and explanation
  RE-->>CK: Version, clock, matched row, explanation, masked fields as hash
